      "children": []
    },
    "b-55-kgr-35s-discovery": {
      "id": "b-55-kgr-35s-discovery",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Discovery is the point of the attachments: a worker on a target sweeps its search indexes — opseq analogs, ghidra, siblings, crosswalk — plus the code graph's call edges to reach related targets, and each related target carries its slice of the attempt ledger and its knowledge. That is how tactics and knowledge recorded elsewhere become discoverable for the current target. No second search system exists: the graph is the spine, plus keyword search over the wiki mirror."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
